  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington crushed yesterday\u201422% revenue growth on actual performance (DOW-adjusted, still +3.3% vs expectation). Core grooming drove it with a 12% lift week-over-week, and retail spiked 73%, signaling front-of-house is leaning into upsells and checkout. You should be proud: year-to-date you're +45% revenue and +44% appointments versus last year. The operational story: you've doubled groomer capacity month-over-month (6/day vs 3/day in August), and your team is holding steady at $459/groomer versus a $466 baseline\u2014that's peak season staffing working correctly. One watch item: add-on attach dropped from 57% to 48%, and bather hours yesterday were zero. This matters. Bathers are a productivity multiplier for groomers and a natural upsell lever; zero hours is likely a scheduling gap, not demand. Restock X-Small Treat Tables and Shanti's Medical Journey immediately\u2014both are deeply negative and eating margin.\n\nHicksville is mixed. Yesterday's 11% revenue dip masks a real operational signal: grooming revenue fell 16% (down $224), but retail exploded 534% and appointment count jumped 57%. Your three groomers produced $425 each, beating the $414 baseline\u2014they're running hot\u2014but add-on attach cratered from 46% to 33%, and you're still running zero bather hours. This store needs bather support and upsell discipline. The bright spot: September appointments are up 114% month-over-month; you're building momentum. Inventory is critical at both locations: X-Small Treat Tables are hemorrhaging stock (negative inventory at both stores); Hicksville's treat shortages (-144 on Treat Table, -78 on Cannoli) will start hitting retail upside if you don't reorder this week.\n\nPattern across both stores: bather capacity is the constraint. Port has 5.8h trailing average with yesterday at zero; Hicksville has zero scheduled bather hours across the entire next 7 days. Bathers unlock groomer throughput and attach revenue. This is structural underutilization of a high-leverage resource.\n\nPort Washington today: 6 groomers, 15 bather hours; Hicksville today: 3 groomers, 0 bather hours; next 7 days: Port 37 groomer-days (76h bathers), Hicksville 17 groomer-days (0h bathers)."
